{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and exquisite cuisine. My recent trip delivered on all fronts, and then some!\n\nTokyo was a sensory overload – neon lights, incredible food stalls in Shinjuku, and the serene Meiji Jingu Shrine offering a peaceful escape. I spent hours wandering through Shibuya crossing, mesmerized by the organized chaos.\n\nKyoto felt like stepping back in time. Geishas gracefully glided through Gion, and the golden Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion) shimmered on the water. I participated in a traditional tea ceremony, a truly calming and insightful experience.\n\nFood was a highlight! From slurping down ramen in Osaka to indulging in delicate sushi in Tokyo, every meal was a delight. Don't even get me started on the matcha everything!\n\nNavigating the public transport was surprisingly easy, and the politeness of the Japanese people was truly remarkable. I even managed to master a few basic Japanese phrases (arigato!).\n\nIt wasn’t always easy – language barriers presented challenges, and getting lost was a frequent occurrence. But those moments of disorientation often led to unexpected discoveries.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions seamlessly interwoven with modern innovation. It’s a place that stays with you long after you’ve left. Highly recommended!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16028544306755066}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015997005393728614}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968666315078735}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.09033963084220886}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.19033394753932953}, {"token": "Japan", "logpro